progress/app-replan/p0\logs\G-perf.jsonl:9:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw progress/app-replan/p0/logs/G-perf.jsonl; Get-Content -Raw progress/app-replan/p0/logs/G-perf.err; Get-Content -Raw tools/build-launch.js; Get-Content -Raw app/index.html'","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a0d836-8c50-7303-ab4f-0412449e7f0d\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Iâ€™ll follow the G-perf brief exactly and limit the write to its specified output file.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"\\\"C:\\\\\\\\Windows\\\\\\\\System32\\\\\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\\\\\v1.0\\\\\\\\powershell.exe\\\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw AGENTS.md; Get-Content -Raw progress/app-replan/p0/p0-diagnose-brief.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"\\\"C:\\\\\\\\Windows\\\\\\\\System32\\\\\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\\\\\v1.0\\\\\\\\powershell.exe\\\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw AGENTS.md; Get-Content -Raw progress/app-replan/p0/p0-diagnose-brief.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# AGENTS.md Ã¢â‚¬â€ Herophilus\\n\\nRules for any agent run from this directory. They bind before any prompt is read; a prompt may\\nnarrow them, never loosen them.\\n\\n1. Read-only unless the brief says otherwise. **Never write anywhere under `app\\\\`** Ã¢â‚¬â€ `app\\\\data\\\\`\\n   above all; that is the live app.\\n   **App-lane exception (owner 2026-09-20):** a brief under `progress\\\\app-replan\\\\` may open\\n   `app\\\\css\\\\`, `app\\\\js\\\\` and `app\\\\index.html` for writing, and only the files it names under\\n   \\\"May change\\\". `app\\\\data\\\\` stays closed Ã¢â‚¬â€ never open it, never write it. Running\\n   `node tools\\\\boot-check\\\\*.js` and `node tools\\\\dist-check.js` is allowed on that lane.\\n2. **Never modify, rename, move or delete anything in `Semester 8\\\\`.** Never copy a scanned page\\n   off this machine. Rendered PNGs live in the session scratchpad only.\\n3. **`key` is a zero-based index into `opts`, never a letter.** `null` if unreadable Ã¢â‚¬â€ never guess.\\n4. **Verbatim means verbatim:** no corrected spelling, units, grammar or abbreviations, no reordered\\n   options, even where the page is plainly wrong.\\n5. **Numbers, units, doses and exponents are transcribed, never normalised.** Anything not\\n   unambiguous at the given resolution goes in `note` instead of being read confidently.\\n6. **A defective printed key is recorded, never disputed and never corrected.**\\n7. **Figures: modality and view only.** Never interpret one, and never let a description answer\\n   the question it belongs to.\\n8. Where the brief lets you write, write results to disk as you go. **A partial job reported\\n   honestly is a success.**\\n9. **On ambiguity, stop and hand back** Ã¢â‚¬â€ do not decide.\\n10. Output is data awaiting a human check. **Never assert that a fact is verified.**\\n11. Never run git Ã¢â‚¬â€ except, on the app lane, read-only `git diff` and `git status`. No network beyond the model call itself.\\n12. **Begin every final reply with the exact line `AGENTS.md loaded Ã¢â‚¬â€ Herophilus`.** The runner\\n    checks for it; a reply without it is discarded.\\n\\r\\n# P0 brief, round 1: diagnose only (2026-09-25)\\n\\nSeat: Codex `gpt-5.6-terra`, one run per item, 900 s clock. Reviewer: Claude Opus refuter.\\nPlan: `progress\\\\PLAN-app-master-2026-09.md` Ã‚Â§5 P0 and Ã‚Â§8 P0.\\n\\n## Marching orders (every item)\\n\\n- Goal: find the ROOT CAUSE of your item and propose the fix. **Round 1 changes no app code.**\\n- May change: ONLY `progress\\\\app-replan\\\\p0\\\\<ITEM>.md` (your findings file). Nothing else, anywhere.\\n- May read: `app\\\\js\\\\`, `app\\\\css\\\\`, `app\\\\index.html`, `tools\\\\`, `progress\\\\`. **`app\\\\data\\\\` stays\\n  closed** (AGENTS.md rule 1): never open, grep or write it.\\n- May run: `node tools\\\\boot-check\\\\*.js`, `node tools\\\\dist-check.js`, read-only `git diff`/`git status`.\\n  Run each check at least twice before calling a failure stable; a flake is a finding.\\n- Must verify: every claim cites `file:line` you actually read, or a command you actually ran plus\\n  its output (trimmed). A cause you could not confirm is marked UNCONFIRMED, never stated as fact.\\n- Do not: edit `app\\\\`, run git writes, touch `Semester 8\\\\`, use the network beyond the model call,\\n  \\\"fix\\\" a check by loosening it without writing why the old assertion was wrong.\\n- Output: `progress\\\\app-replan\\\\p0\\\\<ITEM>.md`, Ã¢â€°Â¤ 80 lines, these headings exactly:\\n  `Symptom (measured)` Ã‚Â· `Root cause` Ã‚Â· `Evidence` Ã‚Â· `Proposed fix` (a diff sketch, files named) Ã‚Â·\\n  `Check that proves the fix` Ã‚Â· `Unconfirmed`.\\n- A partial answer reported honestly is a success. On ambiguity, stop and write what blocks you.\\n- Final reply begins with `AGENTS.md loaded Ã¢â‚¬â€ Herophilus`, then Ã¢â€°Â¤ 5 lines.\\n\\n## Facts already known\\n\\n- `lock-check`, `navclock-check`, `attempt-check` (`tools\\\\boot-check\\\\`) fail **byte-identically\\n  before and after** the B2 split and B12 Ã¢â‚¬â€ pre-existing, never investigated\\n  (`progress\\\\app-replan\\\\plan-until-codex-2026-09-20.md:174-175, 214-216`).\\n- `dist-check` flaked once in three runs, suspected image-copy race (same file :216).\\n- Boot-check baseline 2026-09-20: 0 errors, 4 module cards, QUESTIONS 4049, THEORY 81, 156\\n  chapters. Ophtho unlocked 2026-09-21, neuropsych 2026-09-22 (`LOCKED_MODULES = []`).\\n- Headless Chrome: one at a time; never under a path containing `--`.\\n\\n## Items\\n\\n- **A-checks** Ã¢â‚¬â€ why `lock-check`, `navclock-check`, `attempt-check` fail. Likely one shared cause;\\n  say whether the app or the check is wrong.\\n- **B-dist** Ã¢â‚¬â€ `dist-check` image-copy race: reproduce (run Ã¢â€°Â¥ 5 times), find the race in\\n  `tools\\\\dist-check.js` / `tools\\\\build-launch.js`.\\n- **C-rows** Ã¢â‚¬â€ the ophtho/neuropsych \\\"0-row\\\" report of 2026-09-20 (grep `progress\\\\app-replan\\\\`\\n  for it). Re-measure with boot-check after the unlocks: is it gone? If not, why.\\n- **D-count** Ã¢â‚¬â€ boot-check reports QUESTIONS 4049 while the corpus is ~6.9k. From\\n  `tools\\\\boot-check\\\\boot-check.js` and the loader in `app\\\\index.html` / `app\\\\js\\\\`, explain which\\n  arrays reach `QUESTIONS` and which do not (endpoint files? cases? a lock list?). Do not open\\n  `app\\\\data\\\\`; name the files by the `<script>` tags that load them.\\n- **E-quiz** Ã¢â‚¬â€ two quiz faults, one file: (1) on a 6-option question, pressing `F` while a strike\\n  Ã¢Å“â€¢ has focus is taken as answer letter F (`plan-until-codex-2026-09-20.md:217`); (2) bug c2-1,\\n  `isMdRule` drops an all-punctuation table row like `| - | - |`\\n  (`progress\\\\app-replan\\\\bugs.md:15` and :171). Findings file `E-quiz.md`.\\n- **G-perf** Ã¢â‚¬â€ baseline only, no fix: home first load transfer (bytes of every script/asset\\n  loaded), parse/boot time, peak JS heap, measured with headless Chrome at desktop and with CPU\\n  4Ãƒâ€” slowdown + a slow-3G network profile. Write numbers and the exact method so it can be re-run.\\n  Proposed fix heading: write \\\"none Ã¢â‚¬â€ baseline\\\".\\n\\r\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"\\\"C:\\\\\\\\Windows\\\\\\\\System32\\\\\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\\\\\v1.0\\\\\\\\powershell.exe\\\" -Command \\\"rg --files tools progress/app-replan/p0 app | rg \\\\\\\"(package\\\\\\\\.json|boot-check|launch|perf|index\\\\\\\\.html|\\\\\\\\.js\\\"'$)\\\"; Get-ChildItem -Force | Select-Object -ExpandProperty Name; if (Test-Path package.json) { Get-Content -Raw package.json }'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"\\\"C:\\\\\\\\Windows\\\\\\\\System32\\\\\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\\\\\v1.0\\\\\\\\powershell.exe\\\" -Command \\\"rg --files tools progress/app-replan/p0 app | rg \\\\\\\"(package\\\\\\\\.json|boot-check|launch|perf|index\\\\\\\\.html|\\\\\\\\.js\\\"'$)\\\"; Get-ChildItem -Force | Select-Object -ExpandProperty Name; if (Test-Path package.json) { Get-Content -Raw package.json }'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"app\\\\index.html\\r\\nprogress/app-replan/p0\\\\logs\\\\G-perf.jsonl\\r\\nprogress/app-replan/p0\\\\logs\\\\G-perf.err\\r\\ntools\\\\build-launch.js\\r\\ntools\\\\boot-check\\\\emoji-check.js\\r\\ntools\\\\boot-check\\\\boot-check.js\\r\\ntools\\\\boot-check\\\\b1-shots.js\\r\\ntools\\\\boot-check\\\\attempt-check.js\\r\\ntools\\\\boot-check\\\\strike-check.js\\r\\ntools\\\\boot-check\\\\q2-shots.js\\r\\ntools\\\\boot-check\\\\navclock-check.js\\r\\ntools\\\\boot-check\\\\mobile-check.js\\r\\ntools\\\\boot-check\\\\lock-check.js\\r\\ntools\\\\boot-check\\\\image-check.js\\r\\n.claude\\r\\n.codex\\r\\n.git\\r\\n.impeccable\\r\\n.serena\\r\\napp\\r\\narchive\\r\\nClypsedra\\r\\ncontent\\r\\nDesign\\r\\ndist\\r\\ngenerated\\r\\nprogress\\r\\nSemester 8\\r\\nstyle\\r\\ntools\\r\\n.gitignore\\r\\nAGENTS.md\\r\\nCLAUDE.md\\r\\nerr.log\\r\\nfiles.zip\\r\\ngenerate_t14.py\\r\\nideas-parking.md\\r\\nMEMORY.md\\r\\nREADME.md\\r\\nreference.md\\r\\ns09dump.txt\\r\\ntmp_s08_rows.json\\r\\nverify_t14.js\\r\\nverify_t14.py\\r\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"\\\"C:\\\\\\\\Windows\\\\\\\\System32\\\\\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\\\\\v1.0\\\\\\\\powershell.exe\\\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw progress/app-replan/p0/logs/G-perf.jsonl; Get-Content -Raw progress/app-replan/p0/logs/G-perf.err; Get-Content -Raw tools/build-launch.js; Get-Content -Raw app/index.html'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n\r\nReading additional input from stdin...\n\r\n/* Build the upload-ready dist/ folder for launch, with the two locked\n * subjects' question data genuinely absent â€” not hidden in the client.\n *\n *   node tools/build-launch.js\n *\n * Ophthalmology and Neuropsychiatry are going behind a \"Coming soon\" card for\n * this launch. That has to mean the bytes never leave this machine, not that\n * the client happens not to render them â€” a curious student opening dev\n * tools on the shipped site must not be able to read next month's question\n * bank. So this tool ships a COPY of app/ with those subjects' data files\n * physically removed, never the original app/ folder itself.\n *\n * WHY REMOVING A DATA FILE IS SAFE AT ALL: app/data/questions.js rebuilds one\n * QUESTIONS array from `window.Q_ENT || []`, `window.Q_OPHTHO || []`, etc.,\n * and app/data/theory.js does the same for THEORY with `window.T_* || {}`.\n * Each per-subject file just assigns `var Q_<SUBJECT> = [...]` (classic\n * script, not a module, so it degrades to \"was never loaded\" rather than a\n * ReferenceError) and the aggregator falls back to an empty array/object when\n * that global never got set. This tool does not take that on faith: it reads\n * both aggregators and confirms the `window.<VAR> || fallback` pattern exists\n * for every variable it is about to orphan, and refuses to build if it can't\n * find it. If a future refactor changes that pattern, this tool stops instead\n * of shipping a page that throws on load.\n *\n * WHY FILES ARE DISCOVERED RATHER THAN NAMED: hardcoding\n * \"questions.ophtho.js\" here would silently stop protecting anything the day\n * that file is renamed or a sibling is added. Instead this tool intersects\n * three things every run: the <script src> tags actually present in\n * index.html, the actual directory listing of app/data/, and a simple\n * substring match on the locked subjects' names (which the brief, not this\n * tool, gets to name). Three locked-subject files exist today â€” questions,\n * cases, theory â€” all three are dropped, because \"Coming soon\" means the\n * whole subject is absent, not just its quiz questions; leaving the theory\n * notes in would still ship next month's lecture content in plain text.\n *\n * WHY THE CACHE-BUST HASHES FILE BYTES: this app has no build step and no\n * server-side versioning, so students' browsers will happily keep serving a\n * week-old questions.ent.js from cache after a content fix ships. Hashing the\n * file's own bytes (not the clock) means an unchanged file keeps the same\n * `?v=` and a changed one gets a new one automatically â€” no version number to\n * remember to bump.\n */\n'use strict';\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst crypto = require('crypto');\n\nconst ROOT = path.resolve(__dirname, '..');\nconst APP = path.join(ROOT, 'app');\nconst DIST = path.join(ROOT, 'dist');\nconst INDEX_SRC = path.join(APP, 'index.html');\n\nif (!fs.existsSync(INDEX_SRC)) {\n  console.error('REFUSING: ' + INDEX_SRC + ' not found â€” nothing to build.');\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\n// Named by the brief, not guessed from the filesystem: which two subjects are\n// locked for this launch. Which FILES belong to them is worked out below.\nconst LOCKED_SUBJECTS = []; // neuro unlocked 2026-09-22 (endpoint book closed), ophtho unlocked 2026-09-21, matches LOCKED_MODULES in app/data/modules.js\n\n/* The Theory section as a whole is locked separately from the two locked\n * subjects, and for a different reason: the summaries there are placeholders\n * that the real book chapters will replace, so they are not being published at\n * all yet. The same rule that governs a locked subject governs them â€” \"coming\n * soon\" has to mean the bytes never leave this machine, or a student with dev\n * tools open is reading a draft that was deliberately withheld.\n *\n * The flag is NOT restated here. It is read out of app/data/modules.js, which\n * is where the app itself reads it, so unlocking Theory is still the one-line\n * change it was designed to be and this tool follows it automatically. Parsed\n * without a regex on purpose: the declaration is a single line and a literal\n * scan cannot half-match something that merely mentions the name. */\nfunction readTheoryLocked() {\n  const src = fs.readFileSync(path.join(APP, 'data', 'modules.js'), 'utf8');\n  const marker = 'THEORY_LOCKED';\n  const at = src.indexOf(marker);\n  if (at < 0) return null;\n  const eq = src.indexOf('=', at);\n  const end = src.indexOf(';', eq);\n  if (eq < 0 || end < 0) return null;\n  const value = src.slice(eq + 1, end).trim();\n  if (value === 'true') return true;\n  if (value === 'false') return false;\n  return null;\n}\nconst THEORY_LOCKED = readTheoryLocked();\nif (THEORY_LOCKED === null) {\n  console.error('REFUSING: could not read THEORY_LOCKED out of app/data/modules.js. ' +\n    'It is either gone, renamed, or no longer a plain true/false â€” and this tool cannot ' +\n    'tell whether the theory notes are meant to ship. Fix the flag or this reader; do not guess.');\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\nfunction rmrf(p) { if (fs.existsSync(p)) fs.rmSync(p, { recursive: true, force: true }); }\nfunction copyDir(src, dst) {\n  fs.mkdirSync(dst, { recursive: true });\n  for (const e of fs.readdirSync(src, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n    const s = path.join(src, e.name), d = path.join(dst, e.name);\n    if (e.isDirectory()) copyDir(s, d); else fs.copyFileSync(s, d);\n  }\n}\nfunction walkFiles(dir) {\n  let out = [];\n  for (const e of fs.readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n    const p = path.join(dir, e.name);\n    if (e.isDirectory()) out = out.concat(walkFiles(p));\n    else out.push(p);\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 1. Fresh copy. dist/ is regenerated wholesale every run â€” never patched â€”\n//    so a stale file from a previous build can never survive into a new one.\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\nrmrf(DIST);\ncopyDir(APP, DIST);\nconst INDEX = path.join(DIST, 'index.html');\nlet html = fs.readFileSync(INDEX, 'utf8');\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 2. Work out which data files belong to the locked subjects, by\n//    intersecting index.html's own script tags with app/data's real\n//    directory listing â€” not by naming files up front.\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\nconst dataDirFiles = fs.readdirSync(path.join(APP, 'data'));\n\nconst scriptTagRe = /<script\\b[^>]*\\bsrc=\"([^\"]+)\"[^>]*>\\s*<\\/script>/g;\nconst scriptSrcs = [];\n{ let m; while ((m = scriptTagRe.exec(html))) scriptSrcs.push(m[1]); }\n\nconst excludedRel = new Set();\nfor (const src of scriptSrcs) {\n  if (/^(?:https?:)?\\/\\//.test(src) || src.startsWith('data:')) continue; // no CDN links exist, but never bust one if it did\n  const base = path.basename(src);\n  if (!dataDirFiles.includes(base)) continue; // only touching files that really live in app/data\n  if (LOCKED_SUBJECTS.some(k => base.toLowerCase().includes(k))) excludedRel.add(src);\n  // Every per-subject theory file while the section is locked â€” but never\n  // theory.js itself, which is the aggregator the app still needs in order to\n  // build an empty THEORY map rather than throw.\n  if (THEORY_LOCKED && base !== 'theory.js' &&\n      base.toLowerCase().startsWith('theory.') && base.toLowerCase().endsWith('.js')) {\n    excludedRel.add(src);\n  }\n}\n\n// Same refusal as the locked subjects get, for the same reason: if the section\n// is locked and nothing matched, the naming changed and this tool no longer\n// knows what it is meant to be withholding.\nif (THEORY_LOCKED) {\n  const theoryHits = [...excludedRel].filter(r => path.basename(r) !== 'theory.js' &&\n    path.basename(r).toLowerCase().startsWith('theory.'));\n  if (!theoryHits.length) {\n    console.error('REFUSING: THEORY_LOCKED is true, but no per-subject theory file was found ' +\n      'among the <script src> tags in index.html. Either those files were renamed, or they are ' +\n      'genuinely gone; either way the exclusion cannot be confirmed and will not be guessed.');\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n}\n\n// The constraint that matters most here: if a locked subject turns out to\n// have NO matching file, that is not \"nothing to exclude\" â€” it means the\n// naming scheme changed and this tool no longer knows what to drop. Refuse\n// rather than ship the subject's data by accident.\nfor (const subj of LOCKED_SUBJECTS) {\n  const hit = [...excludedRel].some(r => path.basename(r).toLowerCase().includes(subj));\n  if (!hit) {\n    console.error('REFUSING: no data file found for locked subject \"' + subj + '\" â€” ' +\n      'checked every <script src> in index.html against the app/data/ listing and found ' +\n      'nothing matching. Either the subject\\'s file was renamed, or it is genuinely gone; ' +\n      'either way this tool cannot confirm the exclusion and will not guess.');\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 3. Confirm the graceful-degradation design before relying on it. Each\n//    excluded file declares one `var NAME = ...`; each aggregator must read\n//    `window.NAME || <empty>` for that same NAME, or removing the file would\n//    throw instead of quietly shipping nothing for that subject.\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\nfunction declaredVarName(absPath) {\n  const src = fs.readFileSync(absPath, 'utf8');\n  const m = src.match(/\\bvar\\s+([A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\\s*=/);\n  return m ? m[1] : null;\n}\nconst AGGREGATORS = ['questions.js', 'theory.js'].map(f => path.join(APP, 'data', f));\nconst aggregatorSrc = AGGREGATORS.map(f => fs.readFileSync(f, 'utf8')).join('\\n');\n\nconst designFailures = [];\nfor (const rel of excludedRel) {\n  const abs = path.join(APP, rel);\n  const varName = declaredVarName(abs);\n  if (!varName) {\n    designFailures.push(rel + ': found no top-level \"var NAME = ...\" to check â€” cannot confirm it degrades safely.');\n    continue;\n  }\n  const fallbackRe = new RegExp('window\\\\.' + varName + '\\\\s*\\\\|\\\\|\\\\s*(?:\\\\[\\\\]|\\\\{\\\\})');\n  if (!fallbackRe.test(aggregatorSrc)) {\n    designFailures.push(rel + ' declares ' + varName + ', but neither questions.js nor theory.js ' +\n      'reads \"window.' + varName + ' || []\" / \"|| {}\" â€” removing this file would leave a dangling ' +\n      'reference instead of an empty subject.');\n  }\n}\nif (designFailures.length) {\n  console.error('REFUSING: the graceful-degradation design could not be confirmed for what would be excluded:');\n  designFailures.forEach(f => console.error('  - ' + f));\n  console.error('Fix the aggregator (or this check) before building â€” shipping on an unconfirmed assumption here is the one failure that matters.');\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 4. Remove the excluded files and their <script> tags.\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\nconst excludedReport = [];\nfor (const rel of excludedRel) {\n  const distAbs = path.join(DIST, rel);\n  let bytes = 0;\n  try { bytes = fs.statSync(distAbs).size; } catch (e) { /* already gone is fine */ }\n  fs.rmSync(distAbs, { force: true });\n  const escaped = rel.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\\\$&');\n  const tagRe = new RegExp('[ \\\\t]*<script\\\\b[^>]*\\\\bsrc=\"' + escaped + '\"[^>]*>\\\\s*<\\\\/script>\\\\r?\\\\n?', 'g');\n  html = html.replace(tagRe, '');\n  excludedReport.push({ file: rel, bytes });\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 5. Drop image assets that ONLY the excluded subjects reference. This is\n//    only done where it can be checked reliably: every app/data/*.js file is\n//    scanned for the literal `image:'name'` field (the only form the schema\n//    uses â€” no computed image names exist in this codebase, confirmed by\n//    grep before writing this tool), and a name is dropped only if EVERY\n//    reference to it came from an excluded file. One reference from a kept\n//    subject is enough to keep the image shipped.\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\nconst imgRe = /image\\s*:\\s*['\"]([^'\"]+)['\"]/g;\nconst keptImageNames = new Set();\nconst excludedImageNames = new Set();\nfor (const f of dataDirFiles) {\n  if (!f.endsWith('.js')) continue;\n  const isExcludedFile = [...excludedRel].some(rel => path.basename(rel) === f);\n  const src = fs.readFileSync(path.join(APP, 'data', f), 'utf8');\n  let im;\n  while ((im = imgRe.exec(src))) {\n    (isExcludedFile ? excludedImageNames : keptImageNames).add(im[1]);\n  }\n}\nconst imagesToDrop = [...excludedImageNames].filter(n => !keptImageNames.has(n));\nlet droppedImageBytes = 0, droppedImageCount = 0;\nfor (const name of imagesToDrop) {\n  const p = path.join(DIST, 'assets', 'q', name + '.jpg'); // matches qImgSrc() in index.html\n  if (fs.existsSync(p)) {\n    droppedImageBytes += fs.statSync(p).size;\n    fs.rmSync(p);\n    droppedImageCount++;\n  }\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 6. Cache-bust every remaining local <script src> / <link href> by\n//    appending ?v=<hash of that file's own bytes>, computed AFTER the\n//    excluded files are gone so nothing gets hashed that isn't shipping.\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\nfunction bustAttr(html, tag, attr) {\n  const re = new RegExp('(<' + tag + '\\\\b[^>]*\\\\b' + attr + '=\")([^\"?]+)(\"[^>]*>)', 'g');\n  return html.replace(re, (whole, pre, url, post) => {\n    if (/^(?:https?:)?\\/\\//.test(url) || url.startsWith('data:')) return whole; // no CDN links, but never touch one if it appeared\n    const abs = path.join(DIST, url);\n    if (!fs.existsSync(abs)) return whole; // left as-is; caught by the dangling-reference check below\n    const hash = crypto.createHash('sha1').update(fs.readFileSync(abs)).digest('hex').slice(0, 10);\n    return pre + url + '?v=' + hash + post;\n  });\n}\nhtml = bustAttr(html, 'script', 'src');\nhtml = bustAttr(html, 'link', 'href');\n\nfs.writeFileSync(INDEX, html, 'utf8');\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 7. The one check that must never be skipped: walk the FINAL html for every\n//    local script/link reference and confirm the file is actually there. A\n//    build that ships a page 404ing on its own data file is worse than no\n//    build at all.\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\nfunction collectLocalRefs(html) {\n  const refs = [];\n  const re = /<(?:script|link)\\b[^>]*\\b(?:src|href)=\"([^\"]+)\"/g;\n  let m;\n  while ((m = re.exec(html))) {\n    const url = m[1];\n    if (/^(?:https?:)?\\/\\//.test(url) || url.startsWith('data:')) continue;\n    refs.push(url.split('?')[0]);\n  }\n  return refs;\n}\nconst dangling = collectLocalRefs(html).filter(r => !fs.existsSync(path.join(DIST, r)));\nif (dangling.length) {\n  console.error('REFUSING: dist/index.html references files that are not in dist/ after the build:');\n  dangling.forEach(d => console.error('  - ' + d));\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 8. dist/ must never go to GitHub â€” it is generated, and it is exactly the\n//    kind of folder that \"helpfully\" gets committed once by accident and\n//    then drifts from the source forever. .gitignore is the one existing\n//    file this tool is allowed to touch, and only to append.\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\nconst GITIGNORE = path.join(ROOT, '.gitignore');\nlet gitignoreNote = 'already listed';\nif (fs.existsSync(GITIGNORE)) {\n  const gi = fs.readFileSync(GITIGNORE, 'utf8');\n  if (!/^dist\\/?\\s*$/m.test(gi)) {\n    const sep = gi.endsWith('\\n') ? '' : '\\n';\n    fs.appendFileSync(GITIGNORE,\n      sep + '\\n# Generated by tools/build-launch.js â€” never hand-edited, never committed.\\ndist/\\n');\n    gitignoreNote = 'added';\n  }\n} else {\n  gitignoreNote = 'NOT found â€” could not add dist/ to it';\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 9. Report.\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------\nconsole.log('--- excluded data files (locked subjects: ' + LOCKED_SUBJECTS.join(', ') +\n  (THEORY_LOCKED ? '; plus every theory file, section locked' : '') + ') ---');\nfor (const e of excludedReport) {\n  console.log('  ' + e.file + '  (' + e.bytes.toLocaleString() + ' bytes)');\n}\nconsole.log('  reason: subject is behind \"Coming soon\" for this launch; its questions, cases and');\nconsole.log('  theory notes must be genuinely absent from the upload, not just unlinked in the UI.');\nif (THEORY_LOCKED) {\n  console.log('  theory: THEORY_LOCKED is true in app/data/modules.js, so the summaries are');\n  console.log('  withheld whole â€” they are placeholders for the real book chapters and are not');\n  console.log('  being published yet. theory.js itself still ships, and builds an empty map.');\n}\n\nconsole.log('\\n--- excluded image assets (referenced only by the excluded subjects) ---');\nif (droppedImageCount) {\n  console.log('  ' + droppedImageCount + ' file(s), ' + droppedImageBytes.toLocaleString() + ' bytes total');\n} else {\n  console.log('  none â€” every image the locked subjects reference is also used by a shipping subject, or none exist');\n}\n\nconst files = walkFiles(DIST);\nconst totalBytes = files.reduce((a, f) => a + fs.statSync(f).size, 0);\nconsole.log('\\n--- dist/ ---');\nconsole.log('  ' + files.length + ' files, ' + totalBytes.toLocaleString() + ' bytes total');\nconst largest = files\n  .map(f => ({ f: path.relative(DIST, f), size: fs.statSync(f).size }))\n  .sort((a, b) => b.size - a.size)\n  .slice(0, 10);\nconsole.log('  largest 10:');\nlargest.forEach(x => console.log('    ' + x.size.toLocaleString().padStart(12) + '  ' + x.f));\n\nconsole.log('\\n.gitignore: dist/ ' + gitignoreNote);\n\nconsole.log('\\n=== READY TO UPLOAD: dist/ is the folder the host serves. ===');\n\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" href=\"assets/icon-180.png\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" href=\"data:image/png;base64,\">\n<meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\">\n<meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-title\" content=\"Herophilus\">\n<meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\" content=\"black-translucent\">\n<meta name=\"mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#070d16\">\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Herophilus â€” clinical question bank and revision schedule\">\n<title>Herophilus â€” 2nd Term Question Bank</title>\n<!-- Theme is chosen BEFORE any CSS parses, so a light-mode user never sees a\n     dark flash on load. It has to be inline and it has to be here: a deferred\n     script, or one at the end of <body>, runs after first paint and the flash\n     is then unavoidable. Kept deliberately tiny for the same reason.\n     No stored choice = follow the operating system. -->\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var t=null;\n  try{t=localStorage.getItem('wardround.theme')}catch(e){}\n  if(t!=='light'&&t!=='dark'){\n    t=(window.matchMedia&&matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme:light)').matches)?'light':'dark';\n  }\n  document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme',t);\n})();\n</script>\n<!-- Classical faces, embedded as data URIs. Must sit HERE, in <head> and before\n     the stylesheet: a classic script blocks parsing and runs immediately, so the\n     @font-face rules are registered before first paint. Moved to the end of\n     <body> with the other data files, the whole page would render in a fallback\n     face and then reflow. See data/fonts.js for why they are base64 and not\n     .woff2 files sitting next door. -->\n<script src=\"data/fonts.js\"></script>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"css/tokens.css\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"css/base.css\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"css/layout.css\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"css/components.css\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"css/print.css\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"css/views.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- Ambient colour field. Fixed and non-interactive, sits behind .app.\n     Its motion is paused by CSS on the reading views â€” see the cinematic layer.\n     Source order IS the stacking order here (all children are absolute, none\n     carries a z-index): film at the back, orbs tinting it, scrim over both. -->\n<div class=\"ambient\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n  <!-- muted + playsinline are what make autoplay legal at all; without both,\n       iOS Safari refuses and we fall back to the poster frame, which is a\n       perfectly good still. A failure here costs atmosphere, never function. -->\n  <video class=\"film\" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload=\"auto\"\n         poster=\"assets/ambient-library.jpg\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n    <source src=\"assets/ambient-library.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\">\n  </video>\n  <span class=\"orb o1\"></span><span class=\"orb o2\"></span>\n  <span class=\"orb o3\"></span><span class=\"orb o4\"></span>\n  <span class=\"film-scrim\"></span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"app\">\n  <aside class=\"rail\" id=\"rail\">\n    <div class=\"rail-head\">\n      <div class=\"logo\"><span class=\"blip\"><img src=\"assets/icon-96.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"></span> Herophilus</div>\n      <div class=\"rail-sub\" id=\"railTerm\">Choose your semester</div>\n    </div>\n    <button class=\"railprof\" id=\"railProf\" onclick=\"switchProfile()\"></button>\n    <div class=\"railsync\" id=\"railSync\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n    <div class=\"streak\" id=\"streakBox\"></div>\n    <nav class=\"nav\" id=\"nav\"></nav>\n  </aside>\n\n  <div class=\"main\">\n    <header class=\"topbar\">\n      <button class=\"tb-btn mobile-only\" onclick=\"toggleRail()\" aria-label=\"Menu\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.55\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 7h16M4 12h16M4 17h16\"/></svg></button>\n      <div class=\"search-wrap\">\n        <span class=\"search-ic\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M11 11m-7 0a7 7 0 1 0 14 0a7 7 0 1 0-14 0\"/><path d=\"M20 20l-4.2-4.2\"/></svg></span>\n        <input class=\"search\" id=\"search\" placeholder=\"Search questions, topics, explanationsâ€¦\" autocomplete=\"off\" role=\"combobox\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-autocomplete=\"list\" aria-controls=\"results\">\n        <div class=\"results\" id=\"results\" role=\"listbox\" aria-label=\"Search results\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"topbar-actions\">\n        <button class=\"tb-btn themebtn\" onclick=\"toggleTheme()\"></button>\n        <button class=\"tb-btn kbd-btn\" onclick=\"showShortcuts()\" title=\"Keyboard shortcuts\" aria-label=\"Keyboard shortcuts\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M2.5 6.5h19v11h-19z\"/><path d=\"M6 10h.01M10 10h.01M14 10h.01M18 10h.01M7 14h10\"/></svg></button>\n        <!-- Backup used to be a pair of Export / Import buttons the user had to\n             remember to press. It is automatic now: this is a status light that\n             opens the snapshot list. The file input stays as the rescue path. -->\n        <button class=\"tb-btn bak-btn\" id=\"bakBtn\" onclick=\"showBackup()\"\n                title=\"Backup\" aria-label=\"Backup\"></button>\n        <input type=\"file\" id=\"importFile\" accept=\".json\" style=\"display:none\" onchange=\"importData(event)\">\n      </div>\n    </header>\n    <main class=\"page\" id=\"page\"></main>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"splash\" id=\"splash\">\n  <div class=\"glogo\"><span class=\"blip\"><img src=\"assets/icon-96.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\"></span> Herophilus</div>\n  <div class=\"spinner\"></div>\n  <div class=\"msg\" id=\"splashMsg\">Restoring your session&hellip;</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"gate\" id=\"gate\"></div>\n<!-- The Clepsydra. Empty here and filled by clepMount(): the dial's ticks and\n     the laurel are computed rather than hand-written, so the figure lives in\n     JS beside the maths that places it. -->\n<div class=\"clep\" id=\"clep\" hidden></div>\n<div class=\"toast\" id=\"toast\"></div>\n<div class=\"modal-bg\" id=\"modalBg\" onclick=\"if(event.target===this)closeModal()\">\n  <div class=\"modal\" id=\"modal\"></div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Data lives in separate files so content can be added without editing the app.\n     Classic scripts (not modules) so they load over file:// without CORS.\n     Order matters: per-subject files before the aggregators that concat them. -->\n<script src=\"data/modules.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/questions.ent.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/questions.peds.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/questions.peds.ep.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/questions.peds.ep2.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/questions.ophtho.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/questions.ophtho.ep.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/questions.ophtho.ep2.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/questions.neuro.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/cases.ent.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/cases.peds.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/cases.ophtho.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/cases.neuro.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/questions.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/theory.ent.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/theory.peds.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/theory.ophtho.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/theory.neuro.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"data/theory.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"js/storage.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"js/icons.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"js/theme.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"js/utils.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"js/theory.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"js/gate.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"js/render.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"js/quiz.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"js/sessions.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"js/clepsydra.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"js/boot.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
progress/app-replan/p0\logs\G-perf.jsonl:11:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content progress/app-replan/p0/logs/G-perf.err -Tail 120; if (Test-Path progress/app-replan/p0/G-perf.md) { Get-Content -Raw progress/app-replan/p0/G-perf.md }; rg -n \"puppeteer|chrome|Performance|heap|tracing|slow.?3G\" tools progress -g \"!app/data/**\"; Get-Command chrome,chrome.exe,msedge,msedge.exe -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object Name,Source'","aggregated_output":"progress\\audit-2026-09-03-silent-defects.md:45:**Kept:** the orphan-chapter check (finding #4) — cheap, exact, and independently reproduced.\nprogress\\css-volume-audit.md:248:Single declaration. KEEP. The rail is 238px wide and the right edge of it is the seam between navigation and content; a 3px hard rule is the cheapest way to draw that seam in a way that survives both themes.\nprogress\\css-volume-audit.md:324:The brief counted 23 transitions plus one duplicate at 1684 — verified. Eight of those 23 are doing nothing the overshoot helps; flattening them is the cheapest single change in this report.\nprogress\\css-volume-audit.md:441:Why third: 29 declarations of `border:2.5px solid var(--line-2)` is more than any other single device. They are all the same value, and they are all on surfaces that already carry a shadow. Halving the border weight removes a visible chrome from every card, row, option, button and chip on the page, without changing anything else.\nprogress\\briefs\\ocr-gate-debate-verdict.md:20:**Dropped negation, likelihood and a cheap catch.** You will not estimate likelihood from n=43 with zero numeric/negation-rich items. In Tesseract, short-word deletion is a standard error class; in MCQs, negation is a standard discourse class. Treat the intersection as **expected**, not theoretical.\nprogress\\briefs\\ocr-gate-debate-verdict.md:22:Cheap checks that actually bite, in order of cost:\nprogress\\briefs\\ocr-gate-debate-verdict.md:62:Key blocks are tiny. Vision on a tight crop is cheap. **Visual-always for keys.** If you refuse that, require two independent reads (OCR letter ∩ vision letter) and still human-spot-check a sample. There is no world where a single Tesseract A–E token should be allowed to teach the answer.\nprogress\\briefs\\ocr-gate-debate-verdict.md:75:If “any digit → visual” kills the cost case, the cost case was assuming the hard pages would take the cheap path. They should not.\nprogress\\briefs\\ocr-gate-debate-verdict.md:83:Worth introducing **after** a demonstrated leak, or as a cheap disagreement tripwire **in addition to** forced vision on numbers/keys — never instead of it. The cheaper control you already have is the 300 DPI image you rendered to run Tesseract. **Stop throwing it away on the “success” path.**\nprogress\\briefs\\ocr-gate-debate-verdict.md:120:**ADOPT-WITH-CHANGES** — (1) keys visual-always, (2) never text-only: OCR+image on the “success” path with copy-or-escalate, (3) digits/units/Greek cannot take a cheap path until print-checked, (4) end-to-end vs print on a real holdout, (5) dangerous-token + density gate instead of mean≥88, (6) 300 DPI color fallback.\nprogress\\briefs\\START-HERE.md:344:## 9. Scope — the whole module, in the cheapest order\nprogress\\briefs\\START-HERE.md:624:> AGAINST ITS NOTES AND PATCH THE GAPS.** This is cheap — it is a diff, not a rewrite — and it is\nprogress\\briefs\\START-HERE.md:743:> So tabulating makes a chapter look **cheaper in words and more expensive in pages**, and prose does\nprogress\\briefs\\START-HERE.md:1252:> found everything promised present and nothing uncollected. **The verification is cheap — one\nprogress\\app-replan\\code-map.md:46:| Theme / decorative chrome | 2318–2479 |\ntools\\kbd-probe\\kbd-probe.js:27:const CHROME = 'C:/Program Files/Google/Chrome/Application/chrome.exe';\ntools\\kbd-probe\\kbd-probe.js:323:  const udd