 ms\nprogress\\app-replan\\code-map.md.bak.pre-claude-patch:40:| Theme / decorative chrome | 2318–2480 |\nprogress\\app-replan\\research-living-scene\\debate-r2-fable.md:7:1. Scene reads as a pulse (A:6-9): CONCEDE, same as F:10. Converge on a flame that changes shape, light that moves the pixels (my two-plate crossfade is Astra's \"object-specific light response\" done cheaply), one candle origin, no cursor light, no dust, no camera drift.\nprogress\\app-replan\\research-living-scene\\debate-r2-fable.md:42:1. First flame challenger. Fable: a DOM flame on transform keyframes costs zero JS and stays on the compositor, so battery and main thread stay free; canvas only if it looks like paper cut-outs. Astra: a Canvas 2D procedural flame straight after CSS, because shape variety is what sells a flame and a small canvas is cheap. Settled by: both built on the same plate, owner picks by eye, DevTools trace records main-thread scripting for each.\nprogress\\app-replan\\research-a-to-z\\BRIEF-COMMON.md:41:  costed OPTIONS across a range, cheapest and closest-to-her-current-2D-look first; do not jump straight\nprogress\\app-replan\\research-a-to-z\\f22-offline-install-pwa.md.bak.gate-fix:76:   Strategy choice per Chrome's Workbox strategy guide (https://developer.chrome.com/docs/workbox/caching-strategies-overview, verified): shell files and the question-data files are cache-first/cache-only since they are versioned by `CACHE_VERSION`, not by content hash; `index.html` itself should be network-first in a later iteration if the owner wants same-day content fixes to reach open tabs without a manual reload — flagged as a refinement, not required for v1.\nprogress\\app-replan\\research-living-scene\\debate-r1-fable.md:14:3. The P1 gate is not measurable as written. (a) f7 section 4.1 shows the rAF-delta logger returning 16.67 ms for every variant except one: the method is vsync-capped and sees only outright dropped frames, never GPU headroom, which is the Intel and battery question. (b) rAF runs on the main thread; CSS opacity animations run on the compositor, so the logger does not measure the thing being gated. (c) \"no idle scripting\" contradicts a logger that scripts every frame. (d) f7 line 130: headless run, \"GPU raster state unknown, RTX 3050 vs Intel UHD not distinguished\"; headless Edge has no display vsync (REASONING), so p95 from headless says nothing about the owner's screen. (e) \"zero gaps over 34 ms in 60 s\" on Windows is flaky: one Defender tick fails it. Fix: run headed Edge (the double-clicked file), Windows per-app GPU setting for both GPUs; gate on the DevTools Performance frames track (dropped frames) and Task Manager GPU busy percent, recorded for both GPUs with no numeric threshold until measured; allow at most 2 isolated long frames per minute; keep p95 as a secondary figure. Reduced motion and hidden tab become exact checks: `document.getAnimations().length === 0` when reduced motion is on or the candle is snuffed; hidden tab produces 0 frames. Headless is fine for the contrast screenshots only.\nprogress\\app-replan\\research-a-to-z\\f22-offline-install-pwa.md:89:   Strategy choice per Chrome's Workbox strategy guide (https://developer.chrome.com/docs/workbox/caching-strategies-overview, verified): shell files and the question-data files are cache-first/cache-only since they are versioned by `CACHE_VERSION`, not by content hash; `index.html` itself should be network-first in a later iteration if the owner wants same-day content fixes to reach open tabs without a manual reload — flagged as a refinement, not required for v1.\nprogress\\app-replan\\research-living-scene\\debate-r1-astra.md:26:Fix ? REASONING: After the Neuro gate, agree on a single composition sketch with home, subject, light-theme and narrow crops; resolve the flame treatment and genuine owner guesses together. Run cheap capability probes with a synthetic asset, then create or select the approved plate, then run the visual/performance comparison