\\\\n165:   pipes, dashes, colons and spaces, and it must contain a dash; test for\\\\r\\\\n166:   exactly that. */\\\\r\\\\n167:function isMdRule(row){\\\\r\\\\n168:  const t=String(row).trim();\\\\r\\\\n169:  return /^[|\\\\\\\\s:-]+$/.test(t)&&t.indexOf('-')>=0;\\\\r\\\\n170:}\\\\r\\\\n171:/* âš ï¸ SPLIT A PIPE-TABLE ROW WITHOUT LOSING ITS EMPTY CELLS. The old code was\\\\r\\\\n172:   `row.split('|').filter(c=>c.trim()!=='')`, which drops the two empty\\\\r\\\\n173:   fragments either side of the row â€” and every empty cell INSIDE it too. A\\\\r\\\\n174:   comparison table's header almost always starts with a blank corner cell\\\\r\\\\n175:   (`| | **A** | **B** |`), so its header came out one column short and every\\\\r\\\\n176:   column label shifted left by one against the body. Found by rendering a\\\\r\\\\n177:   two-column comparison to PDF and reading it; nothing throws, and the table\\\\r\\\\n178:   still looks like a table. Trim only the outer delimiters. */\\\\r\\\\n179:/* âš ï¸âš ï¸ THE HEADER ROW GOES IN A <thead>, AND IT IS A PRINT DECISION, NOT TIDINESS.\\\\r\\\\n180:   Measured: compressing a chapter from prose into tables cut its word count by\\\\r\\\\n181:   63 % and its PAGE count by nothing at all â€” 3,826 words still printed 16\\\\r\\\\n182:   pages, where the 10,384-word prose version printed 30. Density fell from ~350\\\\r\\\\n183:   words a page to ~240. The cause is `break-inside:avoid` on a page full of\\\\r\\\\n184:   medium tables: a ten-row table that will not fit in the space left jumps\\\\r\\\\n185:   whole to the next page and leaves the bottom third of the sheet blank, over\\\\r\\\\n186:   and over. Letting tables break is only safe if the reader can still see the\\\\r\\\\n187:   column labels on the continuation page, and `display:table-header-group` on a\\\\r\\\\n188:   real <thead> is what repeats them. Emitted here so md() and mdBlock() cannot\\\\r\\\\n189:   drift apart. */\\\\r\\\\n190:function mdTable(rows,attr){\\\\r\\\\n191:  const body=rows.filter(r=>!isMdRule(r)).map(mdCells);\\\\r\\\\n192:  if(!body.length)return '';\\\\r\\\\n193:  const cell=(c,t)=>`<${t}>${c.trim()}</${t}>`;\\\\r\\\\n194:  let t='<table'+(attr||'')+'>';\\\\r\\\\n195:  t+='<thead><tr>'+body[0].map(c=>cell(c,'th')).join('')+'</tr></thead>';\\\\r\\\\n196:  if(body.length>1)t+='<tbody>'+body.slice(1).map(r=>'<tr>'+r.map(c=>cell(c,'td')).join('')+'</tr>').join('')+'</tbody>';\\\\r\\\\n197:  return t+'</table>';\\\\r\\\\n198:}\\\\r\\\\n199:function mdCells(row){\\\\r\\\\n200:  const c=String(row).split('|');\\\\r\\\\n201:  if(c.length&&c[0].trim()==='')c.shift();\\\\r\\\\n202:  if(c.length&&c[c.length-1].trim()==='')c.pop();\\\\r\\\\n203:  return c;\\\\r\\\\n204:}\\\\r\\\\n205:/* The coloured anchor at the head of an entity block or a \\\\\\\"**Term** â€” fact\\\\\\\"\\\\r\\\\n### progress/app-replan/bugs.md\\\\r\\\\n1:# B10 bug list â€” sweep 2026-09-17 (Sonnet, 8 chunks; verified below by Opus refuter)\\\\r\\\\n2:\\\\r\\\\n3:### c1-1 Â· loadState() drops all fallback on a cloud read failure\\\\r\\\\n4:- Line: 2952\\\\r\\\\n5:- Severity: medium\\\\r\\\\n6:- Repro: with Firebase configured, make `window.storage.get(key)` throw (network blip). `loadState()`'s outer `catch` sets `storageMode='cloud'` and returns immediately, never falling through to the second `try` block that reads `localStorage`/`bakNewest()`. User opens the app after a transient network error and sees a fully blank profile (no answers, no schedule) for that session even though a local snapshot exists.\\\\r\\\\n7:- Why: `}catch(e){if(entry===profileLoad&&me===p)storageMode='cloud';return}` exits before the local/backup fallback ladder that follows it, and also mislabels the mode as `'cloud'` despite the read having just failed.\\\\r\\\\n8:- Fix idea: on catch, fall through to the local/backup ladder (set `mode='local'`) instead of returning early.\\\\r\\\\n9:\\\\r\\\\n10:No other bugs found in 2906-3600 for the checked categories: no `bankOf(` misuse (only its definition and the one correct use inside `banksOf`), no `var(--ink)` outside `color:` in this range, no z-index/stacking code here, no unbounded/leaked timers (only one-shot `setTimeout`s, cleared before reuse in `toast()`), no listener bound twice (the single `matchMedia` listener runs once at parse time), cloud-write queue in `save()` correctly serializes per key.\\\\r\\\\n11:\\\\r\\\\n12:\\\\r\\\\n13:# Bugs â€” chunk c2 (app\\\\\\\\index.html lines 3600-4250)\\\\r\\\\n14:\\\\r\\\\n15:### c2-1 Â· Inline markdown table row misclassified as a separator when a cell holds a bare \\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\"\\\\r\\\\n16:- Line: 3654\\\\r\\\\n17:- Severity: medium\\\\r\\\\n18:- Repro: write theory body/explanation markdown with a pipe table row that uses `-` as a\\\\r\\\\n19:  \\\\\\\"not present\\\\\\\"/placeholder cell, e.g. `| Sign | Left | Right |\\\\\\\\n| Pain | + | - |`. Render it\\\\r\\\\n20:  through `mdBlock()` -> `mdTable()`.\\\\r\\\\n21:- Why: `isMdRule` is `/^[|\\\\\\\\s:-]+$/.test(t)&&t.indexOf('-')>=0` â€” a data row built only from `|`,\\\\r\\\\n22:  space, `:` and `-` characters (no letters/digits) matches this and is silently dropped by\\\\r\\\\n23:  `mdTable`'s `rows.filter(r=>!isMdRule(r))`, which also then promotes the following row into the\\\\r\\\\n24:  header. This is the same corner-cell defect the surrounding comments already fixed once, just\\\\r\\\\n25:  triggered by a dash cell instead of a blank one.\\\\r\\\\n26:- Fix idea: require the row to also start with a real separator token (e.g. `-{3,}` or `:-+:`\\\\r\\\\n27:  per cell) rather than accepting a lone `-` anywhere in an all-punctuation row.\\\\r\\\\n28:\\\\r\\\\n29:No other bugs found in 3600-4250 matching the brief's categories (crash, silent data loss,\\\\r\\\\n30:stranded boot, leaked timer, doubled listener, uncleared state, corrupting write, wrong\\\\r\\\\n31:z-index, listener surviving a view change, async race). `chooseTerm`/`activateTerm` close the\\\\r\\\\n32:modal on every path; `bkInit`/`bkMeasure`/`bkPaint` have no listeners or intervals; `loadSDK`\\\\r\\\\n165:\\\\r\\\\n166:## Refuter verdicts 2026-09-17 (Opus)\\\\r\\\\n167:\\\\r\\\\n168:Read-only re-check of every cited line plus its callers. 7 confirmed, 2 wrong, 1 partly wrong.\\\\r\\\\n169:\\\\r\\\\n170:- c1-1 loadState catch â€” CONFIRMED, medium right. Line 2952 does exit before the local/bakNewest ladder and mislabels the mode.\\\\r\\\\n171:- c2-1 isMdRule â€” WRONG AS WRITTEN, low not medium. The quoted row `| Pain | + | - |` cannot match: `/^[|\\\\\\\\s:-]+$/` rejects the letters and the `+`. Only an all-punctuation row like `| - | - |` is dropped. Latent trap, not a live defect.\\\\r\\\\n172:- c3-1 redirect lost when initCloud fails â€” CONFIRMED but INCOMPLETE. `if(!ok)return false` (4469) does precede `getRedirectResult()` (4472), and boot 8293 then defaults to 'signin' (4706). But it needs the 8 s loadSDK timeout to expire, so it does not explain the owner's normal-network report. See sign-in pass.\\\\r\\\\n173:- c4-1 upload vs saveProfile â€” CONFIRMED, medium. `saveProfile()` nulls `draft` (5026), the captured `img.onload` reads `draft.av.c` (5009) and throws.\\\\r\\\\n174:- c4-2 upload attaches to wrong draft â€” CONFIRMED, severity overstated (medium). Same root cause as c4-1; one fix covers both.\\\\r\\\\n### progress/app-replan/plan-until-codex-2026-09-20.md\\\\r\\\\n210:  screen (the desk photo owns the background; never both). Assumption stated to him, not yet\\\\r\\\\n211:  confirmed: big front card = last-used subject, the other three fan beside it.\\\\r\\\\n212:- 2026-09-21 results. B3a-1 icons committed (refuter PASS). B3a-2 copy: no-op, all 12 audit\\\\r\\\\n213:  anchors already gone. B12 strike-out committed `af16306` after two refuter FAILs; the last fix\\\\r\\\\n214:  (strike reset inside `startQuiz`) is machine-checked only. lock-check, navclock-check and\\\\r\\\\n215:  attempt-check fail byte-identically before and after B12 (two refuter runs) - p